ely new suite of tests if we want, but I thought it prudent to get a real integration test in to verify search responses are what we expect (this shows some bugs in my original approach)."],"path":"server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/search/functionscore/QueryRescorerIT.java","id":37388,"created_at":"2024-10-18T03:47:56Z","original_position":71,"side":"RIGHT","position":61,"submitted_on_commit":"c69ddbc920cd83c80ebf8cf6390be9f36ed3b8e5","diff_hunk":"@@ -979,9 +1001,173 @@ public void testRescoreAfterCollapseRandom() throws Exception {\n         });\n     }\n \n+    public void testRescoreWithTimeout() throws Exception {\n+        // no dummy docs since merges can change scores while we run queries.\n+        int numDocs \u003d indexRandomNumbers(\"whitespace\", -1, false);\n+\n+        String intToEnglish \u003d English.intToEnglish(between(0, numDocs - 1));\n+        String query \u003d intToEnglish.split(\" \")[0];\n+        assertResponse(\n+            prepareSearch().setSearchType(SearchType.QUERY_THEN_FETCH)\n+                .setQuery(QueryBuilders.matchQuery(\"field1\", query).operator(Operator.OR))\n+                .setSize(10)\n+                .addRescorer(new QueryRescorerBuilder(new TimedQueryBuilder(500)).windowSize(100))\n+                .setTimeout(TimeValue.timeValueMillis(10)),","submitted_line":1015},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `TimeExceededException` class is now public, which could potentially expose internal exception details to external code. Consider making it package-private if it\u0027s not intended for use outside the package.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/rescore/RescoreContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/rescore/RescoreContext.java--1405:1520","promptId":"#BTNXH","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/rescore/RescoreContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/rescore/RescoreContext.java","srcChanges":[],"